% ============================================================
% Methodology
% ============================================================
\section*{Methodology and Limitations}

This report was generated automatically from the Contract Understanding Atticus Dataset (CUAD) v1, created by The Atticus Project and licensed under CC BY 4.0. The underlying contracts are public SEC EDGAR filings.

Findings are derived from CUAD's expert clause annotations plus a diligence rubric applied to span text. The rubric flags items for attorney review; it does not constitute legal advice and does not opine on whether a clause is favorable or unfavorable to any party.

Known limitations:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.4em,itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{CUAD date normalization.} Some normalized dates in the source dataset contain errors (day/month transposition). Date-derived lifecycle values should be verified against the original contract text.
\item \textbf{Multi-part agreements.} <{ n_multi_part_corpus }> contracts in this corpus are fragments of larger agreements. Absence findings on those contracts are annotated accordingly.
\item \textbf{Redactions.} <{ n_redacted_corpus }> contracts contain redaction markers. Clauses redacted at the SEC filing stage cannot be scored.
\item \textbf{Reference date.} <{ reference_note }>
\end{itemize}

